---
export const title = 'Filters from a sentence';
export const order = 300;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
import DemoScript from '../../../../components/DemoScript.astro';
---

<p>
  With <code>search</code> and a provider that offers <code>parse</code> (ADR-030002), typing a sentence
  offers <strong>Turn into filters</strong>. The provider gets the sentence and the filter definitions,
  never record values, and answers with a value; the bar keeps only known filters with valid values,
  and leaves words it could not map as search text. Type "urgent hardware incidents in Pune" below. The
  demo's provider is scripted.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-filter-bar id='filter-sentence' search search-placeholder='Search incidents' style='inline-size: 100%;'></wc-filter-bar>
  <script type='module' src='/assets/js/ai-demo.js'></script>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var bar = document.querySelector('#filter-sentence');
      bar.filters = [
        { key: 'urgency', label: 'Urgency', type: 'select', options: [{ label: '1 · High', value: '1' }, { label: '2 · Medium', value: '2' }, { label: '3 · Low', value: '3' }] },
        { key: 'category', label: 'Category', type: 'multiselect', options: [{ label: 'Hardware', value: 'hardware' }, { label: 'Software', value: 'software' }] },
        { key: 'location', label: 'Location', type: 'select', options: [{ label: 'Pune', value: 'pune' }, { label: 'London', value: 'london' }] },
        { key: 'mine', label: 'Assigned to me', type: 'boolean' },
      ];
      bar.addEventListener('change', function (event) {
        myConsole.log('change: ' + JSON.stringify(event.detail.value));
      });
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<DemoScript name='ai-demo' />

<h3>Suggested until edited</h3>
<p>
  The new chips are marked with a sparkle, and one Suggested badge sits after them. Its clear button
  puts the previous filters back. Editing or removing a chip makes it the person's own. The table
  reloads from <code>change</code> exactly as if the person had added the filters themselves.
  <code>no-ai</code> turns this off for one bar.
</p>
